language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_041_n_fractions: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Find distinct non-zero digits A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H and I such that A / BC + D / EF + G / HI = 1, where BC, EF and HI are the two-digit numbers formed by B and C, E and F, and H and I.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_041_n_fractions.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ the nine digits of the fractions, each a non-zero digit
find A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I : int(1..9)

branching on [A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I]
such that
$ the nine digits are distinct
allDiff([A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I]),
$ A / BC + D / EF + G / HI = 1, multiplied through by BC * EF * HI so that no division is needed
A * (10 * E + F) * (10 * H + I) + D * (10 * B + C) * (10 * H + I) + G * (10 * B + C) * (10 * E + F) = (10 * B + C) * (10 * E + F) * (10 * H + I)
